.TH STR_ANSILEN 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
str_ansilen \- Calculate the length of an ANSI string

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/str.h>
.IB #include <lib/scan.h>

.IB size_t
.IB str_ansilen(const char* in);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBstr_ansilen\fR function calculates the length of an ANSI string, ignoring ANSI escape sequences. ANSI escape sequences are commonly used for text styling in terminal output.

.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.IB in
The input string containing the ANSI escape sequences.

.SH RETURN VALUE
The function returns the number of characters in the string after ignoring ANSI escape sequences.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBstr_ansilen\fR function:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/str.h>
#include <lib/scan.h>

int main() {
    const char* input = "\x1b[31mHello, World!\x1b[0m";
    size_t len = str_ansilen(input);
    printf("Length without ANSI escape sequences: %zu\n", len);
    return 0;
}
.nef